From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: no Attention row on the Sable page

Sable 2.0: BlackBerry 10 had one notification story, Hub and the per-app
alert settings. Sound, vibration and light are Android's own channel
settings, and the Sable-only outputs are off on the Q25, so the separate
Attention row only linked on. It leaves the Sable page; Hub's Connected
apps now carries the per-app Alerts link instead.
---
 res/xml/sable_settings.xml | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/res/xml/sable_settings.xml b/res/xml/sable_settings.xml
--- a/res/xml/sable_settings.xml
+++ b/res/xml/sable_settings.xml
@@ -50,13 +50,6 @@
         settings:controller="com.android.settings.sable.SableLinkPreferenceController" />
 
     <Preference
-        android:key="sable_attention"
-        android:icon="@drawable/ic_volume_up_filled"
-        android:title="@string/sable_page_attention_title"
-        android:summary="@string/sable_page_attention_summary"
-        settings:controller="com.android.settings.sable.SableLinkPreferenceController" />
-
-    <Preference
         android:key="sable_page_lock"
         android:icon="@drawable/ic_settings_security_filled"
         android:title="@string/sable_page_lock_title"
-- 
2.43.0
